# best-news-rss Overview

Next.js app deployed on **Vercel** that aggregates RSS feeds, cleans them, and serves them to Dakboard (a smart display dashboard).

## Key Files

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `data/feeds.json` | Source of truth for all feed sources (id, name, url) |
| `lib/feeds-store.ts` | Reads/writes feeds.json; writes **fail on Vercel** (read-only FS at runtime) |
| `lib/rss/fetch.ts` | Fetches and cleans individual feeds |
| `lib/rss/merge.ts` | Merges all feeds into one deduplicated, date-sorted list |
| `lib/display/items.ts` | Powers the display widget — different options than RSS routes |
| `app/rss/all/route.ts` | `/rss/all` — merged RSS feed for Dakboard (50 items, fresh per request) |
| `app/api/display/route.ts` | `/api/display` — JSON for the display widget (30 items, cached 5 min) |

## Adding Feeds

**Always edit `data/feeds.json` and commit** — the UI's POST `/api/feeds` tries to write to disk and fails silently on Vercel with a 503. The deployed app only reads what was in the repo at deploy time.

## Two Output Paths with Different Options

| | `/rss/all` and `/rss/[id]` | `/api/display` (widget) |
|--|--|--|
| `maxParagraphs` | 1 (lead sentence only) | 8 (full article body) |
| `dropFullContent` | true | false |
| `excludeSports` | false | true (hardcoded) |
| Caching | fresh per request | ISR, 5-min cache |

This difference in `excludeSports` is the most common source of bugs: something can appear in `/rss/all` but be silently dropped from the display.
